wrote:

>What is the best way to deal with an angered priest (or any other
>peaceful that will give you the "murderer" brand and cost you your
>telepathy)?  By this I mean coaxing him onto a different level or
>somehow incapacitating him/her so that you can use the altar.  Ideally
>I would like to find a way of killing him so that he can be looted.  If
>you polymorph him into another creature then kill him do you still lose
>your telepathy?  If I am not mistaken, the alignment penalty for
>killing peaceful priests is bigger than for other peacefuls.


  Best advice I've read is throw rocks at the priest from outside
the temple.  Dig out one side of the temple first.


  Ring of conflict may be of help.


  Best way to avoid losing telepathy is to be chaotic :-).


  The polymorph trick will probably work, if the priest isn't
wearing a cloak of magic resistance.  There is a small 
probability of that.


  If the priest is co-aligned with you there are other 
considerations.


  Jove


